# Append-only JSONL ledgers: two lanes appending different rows is NOT a conflict.
# Without merge=union, every parallel wave that files an issue conflicts on the ledger and a
# human resolves it by hand -- which is how rows get dropped. D-019 makes the lane shards
# (qa/issues.<lane>.jsonl) shards of ONE ledger, so they need the same treatment as the
# canonical file. Union keeps both sides' lines; it does NOT fix duplicate id ALLOCATION
# (that is D-019's per-lane ISS-<LANE>-NNN rule) -- it only stops the merge itself losing rows.
qa/issues.jsonl        merge=union
qa/issues.*.jsonl      merge=union
qa/token-ledger.jsonl  merge=union
docs/FEATURES.jsonl    merge=union

# ISS-390: byte-pinned inputs of the 72-claim review bundle (index.json -> batch-NN.json -> sourceBinding).
